oth sides and use the addition and scalar multiplication properties of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}-2y} & =L{-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\ L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =-5L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate $L{{y}^{′}},$ we use the formula for the Laplace transform of a derivative and the initial condition $y(0)=1:$\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}=sL{y}-y(0)=sY(s)-1\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,s>0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can solve for $Y(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{y}^{′}}-2L{y} & =-5L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t} \\\\ (sY(s)-1)-2Y(s) & =-5(\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}) \\\\ sY(s)-2Y(s) & =1-\\frac{5}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ (s-2)Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{{s}^{2}+1} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{{s}^{2}-4}{({s}^{2}+1)(s-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s>2,$ we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Y(s) & =\\frac{(s-2)(s+2)}{({s}^{2}+1)(s-2)} \\\\ Y(s) & =\\frac{s+2}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535955 true] [17592186376313 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376314 13194139535955 true] [17592186376313 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376315 13194139535955 true] [17592186376313 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376316 13194139535955 true] [17592186376313 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376317 13194139535955 true] [17592186376313 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376318 13194139535955 true] [17592186376313 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535955 true] [17592186376313 1041 "selection" 13194139535955 true] [17592186376313 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376317 13194139535955 true] [17592186376313 1110 #uuid "6ac1d161-04fb-5d09-ba47-f01cbbfa805a" 13194139535955 true] [17592186376314 1034 "Y(s)=\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}" 13194139535955 true] [17592186376314 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535955 true] [17592186376314 1111 #uuid "cb5658fd-46fe-5fcb-99a4-8688e6af657a" 13194139535955 true] [17592186376315 1034 "Y(s)=\\frac{s+2}{({s}^{2}+1)(s-2)}" 13194139535955 true] [17592186376315 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535955 tr