e standard transform \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{at}}=\\frac{1}{s-a},\\,s>a,\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-1)+2Y(s) & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+3} \\\\ (s+2)Y(s)-1 & =\\frac{5}{s+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ First, add $1$ to the right-hand side and find a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s+2)Y(s) & =1+\\frac{5}{s+3} \\\\ (s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{s+3}{s+3}+\\frac{5}{s+3} \\\\ (s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{s+8}{s+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing by $(s+2),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{s+8}{(s+2)(s+3)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. We write $Y(s)$ in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{s+8}{(s+2)(s+3)}=\\frac{A}{s+2}+\\frac{B}{s+3}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants $A$ and $B,$ we first clear the denominators:\n\n$$\ns+8=A(s+3)+B(s+2)\n$$\n\nNow, we find the constants $A$ and $B.$\n\n- Setting $s=-2,$ we have\n\n$$\n-2+8=A(-2+3)+B(0)\\,⟹\\,6=1A\\,⟹\\,A=6.\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n-3+8=A(0)+B(-3+2)\\,⟹\\,5=-1B\\,⟹\\,B=-5.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{6}{s+2}-\\frac{5}{s+3}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} & ={e}^{-2t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} & ={e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =6{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}-5{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+3}} \\\\ y(t) & =6{e}^{-2t}-5{e}^{-3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535955 true] [17592186376320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376321 13194139535955 true] [17592186376320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376322 13194139535955 true] [17592186376320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376323 13194139535955 true] [17592186376320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376324 13194139535955 true] [17592186376320 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376325 13194139535955 true] [17592186376320 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535955 true] [17592186376320 1041 "field-1" 13194139535955 true] [17592186376320 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376323 1